# Third-party dependencies

This file enumerates third-party libraries and assets that are bundled,
linked, or referenced in Paideia, along with their licenses.

Every production dependency added must appear here. CI enforces this via
scripts/check-licenses.mjs.

## License allowlist (bundled into JS payload)

The following licenses are accepted for code bundled into the browser:
- MIT
- Apache-2.0
- BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause
- ISC
- MPL-2.0 (file-level copyleft only — acceptable when wrapped)
- 0BSD
- Unlicense
- CC0-1.0

## Rejected (cannot bundle into JS payload)

- GPL-*, AGPL-*, LGPL-*, SSPL-*, BUSL-*, commercial-only

These may be used as external services (self-hosted, accessed via iframe or
HTTP) but never bundled. Each such use must be documented in the consuming
package's TECHNICAL.md.

